Draw_Other_Objects (0x42d008), L1 Wild Bill and cigar animation: reconstruct
its contiguous 8-byte angle vector, instead of passing the address of a
standalone DWORD and reading unrelated stack locals as its Z angle.
Original dd2h.exe:
  0x42d02d / 0x42d062: edi = ebp-0x24
  0x42d039-0x42d03a / 0x42d07b-0x42d07c: two movsd copy all 8 source bytes
  0x42d055 / 0x42d097: mov [ebp-0x20],ax replaces only the third SHORT
  0x42d059 / 0x42d09b: lea eax,[ebp-0x24], passed to Draw_Dynamic_Objects
  0x420510: FUN_004204d0 loads angle Z from DWORD[input+2] >> 16.
The decompile split the vector into local_28/local_24/uStack_22 and wrote
its third angle to the unrelated invented global _local_24. Native and
WASM consequently used different adjacent stack bytes when rotating the
Wild Bill mesh. Keep both source DWORDs and replace exactly its Z WORD.
This removes the L1 native/WASM video split without changing culling.

